{
 "benchmark_id": "iec60909-sequence-fault-kernel-v1",
 "tool": "shortcircuit",
 "file": "shortcircuit.html",
 "generator": "bench-src/ref/gen_shortcircuit.py",
 "reference": "Independent Python complex-arithmetic implementation of the cited IEC 60909-0:2016 sequence-fault equations, written in ohms from the published closed forms. It constructs Z1/Z2/Z0 from |Z| and X/R, applies the equivalent voltage source c Un/sqrt3 at the fault point for 3-phase, line-line, line-earth and line-line-earth faults, the Method-C peak factor and the clause 4.8 thermal factor. No JavaScript from shortcircuit.html is imported, transcribed or read; the page solves a per-unit nodal admittance system with a complex sparse LU, this reference forms no matrix.",
 "citations": [
  "IEC 60909-0:2016, clause 4.2 - equivalent voltage source and initial symmetrical short-circuit currents for balanced and unbalanced faults; eq. (29) three-phase, eq. (34) line-to-line, eq. (52) line-to-earth",
  "IEC 60909-0:2016, clause 4.2 - line-to-line short circuit with earth connection: Ik2E'' = c Un |Z0 - a Z2| / |Z1 Z2 + Z1 Z0 + Z2 Z0| and the earth current IkE2E'' = sqrt3 c Un |Z2| / |Z1 Z2 + Z1 Z0 + Z2 Z0|",
  "IEC 60909-0:2016, clause 4.3.1.2, equations (55)-(56) - ip = kappa sqrt(2) Ik'' and kappa = 1.02 + 0.98 exp(-3 R/X), read by Method C at fc = 0.4 f",
  "IEC 60909-0:2016, clause 4.8, equations (68)-(69) - thermal equivalent short-circuit current Ith = Ik'' sqrt(m + n) and the a.c. factor m = [exp(4 f Tk ln(kappa-1)) - 1] / (2 f Tk ln(kappa-1))"
 ],
 "tolerance": {
  "currents": "abs(error) <= 1e-6 A + 1e-10*|reference|",
  "kappa": "abs(error) <= 1e-12",
  "thermal_m": "abs(error) <= 1e-12",
  "basis": "Both implementations evaluate closed-form analytical equations in IEEE-754 double precision; tolerance covers floating-point evaluation order only and is far tighter than the UI display resolution."
 },
 "not_benchmarked": [
  "n, the d.c. factor of eq. (68): clause 4.8 reads it from Figure 23 as a function of Ik''/Ik and Tk, the page takes it as a user input, and so does this reference. What eq. (68) is graded on is the sqrt(m + n) combination with the case's own n.",
  "The breaking current Ib (clause 4.5), the steady-state current Ik (4.6) and the near-generator a.c. decay: the page computes Ib only for a 3-phase maximum case with a source breakdown, and no case here has a machine to decay.",
  "The transformer impedance correction K_T (6.3.3), the motor locked-rotor impedance (6.8) and the transformer zero-sequence vector-group construction: every case here is a Thevenin equivalent with gen and motor off, so the kernel's network mode is untouched by these 12 cases.",
  "The Z_f terms of eq. (34), eq. (52) and the L-L-E form are implemented in this reference and exercised by no case: only the 3-phase case quotes a fault resistance.",
  "IEC 60909-0:2026 is the current edition. This is the 2016 equation set; the edition delta is not verified by this benchmark.",
  "I_res for a 3-phase or line-to-line fault is a structural zero (no earth path in the boundary conditions), not an independently computed quantity. It is graded, because a kernel that leaked a residual current into a balanced fault would be wrong, but a pass there is weaker evidence than a pass on the two earth-fault cases."
 ],
